1. Java comments are text notes written in the code to provide an explanation about the source code.
2. The comments can be used to explain the logic or for documentation purposes.
3. The compiler does not compile the comments.

In Java, comments are very similar to C and C++.
1. Single-line comments
    // comment

2. Multiline comments
    /*
    Comment (line 1)
    Comment (line 2)
    ...
    */

3. Documentation comments
    /**
    * line 1
    * line 2
    ...
    */
